<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Angria</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Engern</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Angria, or Engern, was one of the three main divisions of Old <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a>, between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/westphalia">Westphalia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastphalia">Eastphalia</a> along the middle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/weser">Weser</a> in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, named after the ancient Angrivarii. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a> conquered it in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxon-wars">Saxon Wars</a> of 772–804. In 1180, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-the-lion">Henry the Lion</a>'s duchy was broken up, the title of Duke of Westphalia and Engern passed to the archbishops of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cologne">Cologne</a>.</p></div>
